  "_note": "GE-07: the sim unit's serialized capability view (the 1089 m_Capabilities object a UNIT_CAPABILITIES report carries), used two ways: (1) compile_op.js --caps feeds it to compileOperation as the registry so 'do gpio.led|flash|servo' resolves against the advertised per-pin actions the Phase-1 stub cannot name; (2) the <op>.ctx.json sidecars embed it under registries.<unit> so verify_wrap.js checks do-params and waited-on module events against the same advert (CAP-001/CAP-002). The advert mirrors gpioBuildAdvert() for the sim pin set (modules/templates/de_rpi_gpio.sim.json); the module's wire advert carries no events map (events are per-pin and dynamic) - the entries below describe the documented gpio.<pin>.went_on|went_off|changed surface so the verifier can prove an op's waited-on events have a producer on this unit. PF-03: the dotted `events` map is no longer needed for CAP-001 — <ns>.<key>.<verb> names are checked by CAP-006 against the resource set instead; PF-02's event_patterns replaces this map on the wire. ci/check_library.py parses this file strictly - keep it comment-free.",
